      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1982, the Park Cities Historical Society was founded to preserve the community's heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park_Cities%2C_Texas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Society supports archives at the University Park Library, landmarking, scholarships for HPISD seniors, and a Distinguished Chair for History at Highland Park High School.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://preservationparkcities.org/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A video project records oral histories of long‑standing residents, showcasing how architecture and people shaped Park Cities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://preservationparkcities.org/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Park Cities originated as two planned upscale communities, Highland Park founded in 1913 and University Park incorporated in 1924, surrounded by Dallas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/park_cities_texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area spans roughly 5.93 square miles, remaining fully incorporated without annexation gaps, and sits just four miles north of downtown Dallas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/park_cities_texas",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Highland Park Village, opened in 1931, was the nation’s first planned outdoor shopping center, a landmark of the Park Cities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
